.TH AMB 1 "" "Ambrotype 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amb \- Ambrotype's command\-line tool: develop raws, edit, organise and export photos
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amb
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ambrotype is a free, open\-source photo editor that reads and writes Lightroom's XMP sidecars and presets. \fBamb\fR does from a terminal (or a script, or an AI assistant) what the editor does: every edit goes through the same undoable commands and lands in the photo's sidecar.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B amb preset inspect <FILE>... [\-\-json]
Show what a preset contains and how it maps to our support
.TP
.B amb preset dump <FILE>
Print the parsed settings as JSON
.TP
.B amb preset census <PATH>... [\-\-json]
Count tag usage across a preset collection (dirs are scanned recursively)
.TP
.B amb sweep plan [\-\-groups G,..]
List the Lightroom calibration sweeps
.TP
.B amb sweep generate \-\-out <DIR> [\-\-groups G,..] [\-\-synthetic P,..] [<RAW>...]
Write a sweep kit for importing into Lightroom (docs/lightroom\-trial\-plan.md): raw copies + XMP sidecars, and/or synthetic DNG targets with embedded settings
.TP
.B amb calibration defaults
Print the default model constants as calibration JSON
.TP
.B amb testimage <PATTERN> <OUT.dng>
Write one synthetic target (ramp, hue, edges, colorchecker, negative: a scanned colour negative, dust: a slide with dust)
.TP
.B amb render <RAW> <OUT.jpg|.png|.tif|.webp|.avif|.exr|.jxl> [\-\-preset P] [\-\-amount A] [\-\-look default|linear] [\-\-calibration fitted.json] [\-\-lens\-db DIR] [\-\-lcp\-dir DIR] [export options]
Develop a raw with its own sidecar (or \-\-preset, a preset or another sidecar), export it, and report which settings are not rendered yet
.TP
.B amb render <RAW>... \-\-out\-dir DIR [\-\-format jpeg|...] [\-\-name TEMPLATE] [same options]
The same for many raws (e.g. a folder: photos/*.NEF), with the same preset and export options; one failure doesn't stop the rest. \-\-name names the files as Import does: {name} {yyyy} {mm} {dd} {hh} {min} {ss} {seq} {camera}, e.g. trip_{seq}
.TP
.B amb render <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-out\-dir DIR [\-\-recursive] [\-\-flat] [\-\-skip\-existing] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json] [export options]
Smaller copies of folders full of photos (raws, JPEGs, ...): with \-\-recursive the subfolders' too, in the same folders under DIR (\-\-flat: all in DIR; clashing names get \-2, \-3). A raw with a JPEG of the same name counts once, as the raw. A few at a time; \-\-skip\-existing leaves files that are newer than their photo and its edit, so a stopped run carries on (change DIR when you change the size). Ends with a summary; \-\-dry\-run lists the files
.TP
.B amb do <PHOTO|SIDECAR.xmp> \(dq<EDITS>\(dq [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
Edit in the compact syntax as one undoable step and print only what changed, e.g. \(dqexp=+0.5 con+=10 hl=\-40 reset:hsl preset:film.xmp@50\(dq (Name=v, Name+=d, Name\-=d, reset:X, preset:P[@amount], snap:N, load:N, undo, redo; short names temp tint exp con hl sh wh bl tex cla deh vib sat sharp nr cnr vig grain; docs/ai/core.md)
.TP
.B amb edit <SIDECAR.xmp> \-\-commands <CMDS.json|\-> [\-\-out <NEW.xmp|.json>] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-brief] [\-\-json]
Apply protocol commands (set_param, adjust_param, reset_param, reset_group, apply_preset, add_mask, set_mask, paint_mask, remove_mask, duplicate_mask, move_mask, add_spot, set_spot, remove_spot, undo, redo) as one transaction, print the diff and write the sidecar (other XMP metadata kept)
.TP
.B amb match <PHOTO> <REF>... [\-\-apply] [\-\-parts wb,tone,color,grading,hsl] [\-\-out PRESET.xmp] [\-\-json]
Find the settings that make the photo look like the reference images (JPEGs, or raws with their edits): white balance, tone, Vibrance/Saturation, Color Grading tints and the Color Mixer (HSL per colour), solved on small renders. Shows the changes; \-\-apply makes them one undoable step, \-\-out also writes them as a preset
.TP
.B amb auto <PHOTO> [\-\-tone] [\-\-wb] [\-\-apply] [\-\-out PRESET.xmp] [\-\-json]
Lightroom\-style Auto: the tone sliders (and Vibrance for dull colour) and the white balance (as Auto), from the photo's own look; \-\-tone or \-\-wb for one of them. Shows the changes; \-\-apply makes them one undoable step
.TP
.B amb fuji <RECIPE.txt|\-> [PHOTO] [\-\-sensor S] [\-\-name N] [\-\-out PRESET.xmp] [\-\-apply] [\-\-json]
A Fujifilm\-style camera recipe, pasted as it's written (Film Simulation, Dynamic Range, Highlight, Shadow, Color, Grain Effect, White Balance with its shift…), recreated as develop settings through the Film recipe plugin. \-\-sensor (X\-Trans I to V, Bayer, GFX, or a camera model such as X\-T3) keeps the settings to what those cameras have, when the recipe doesn't say. \-\-out writes it as a preset in the Fuji group; with a PHOTO, \-\-apply puts it on the photo (one undoable step)
.TP
.B amb convert <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-to FOLDER [\-\-look camera|auto|like:PHOTO] [\-\-no\-edits] [\-\-best\-of\-bursts] [export options]
Raws to JPEGs in one go (a card shot in RAW by mistake): camera, the default, gives what the camera would have saved (its own JPEG inside the raw when that is full size, else the raw matched to it); auto, each photo's Auto tone and white balance; like:PHOTO, each matched to the look of one you edited. Auto and like keep their settings in the raws' sidecars (not with \-\-no\-edits). JPEGs already there are kept, so a stopped run carries on. \-\-best\-of\-bursts converts only the best photo of each burst
.TP
.B amb replay <PHOTO> \-\-out REPLAY.mp4 [\-\-long\-edge N] [\-\-no\-captions]
Edit Replay: a short video of the photo's edit from its History, each step easing in and named, the before and the after held; AV1 in MP4, 1080 pixels on the long side by default
.TP
.B amb contact <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-out SHEET.jpg [\-\-style film|plain] [\-\-columns N] [\-\-paper a4|a3|letter|8x10|11x14] [\-\-landscape] [\-\-title TEXT]
Contact sheets at 300 dpi: each photo small with its edit, as strips of 35 mm film (sprocket holes, frame numbers and the title as edge print; 6 frames a strip, a 36\-frame roll on one A4 page) or a plain grid with file names. More photos than fit make pages: SHEET\-001.jpg, ...
.TP
.B amb search <WORDS> <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-json]

.TP
.B amb search \-\-like <PHOTO> <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-json]
Smart search: the photos ranked by what is in them (dog on a beach, snowy mountains), or by likeness to another photo, with the chosen search model (`amb models install clip\-b32`, 156 MB, or siglip2\-base, 690 MB and better). Photos are indexed once (about 0.7 s each) and kept in the catalogue
.TP
.B amb share <PHOTO> \-\-out PAGE.html [\-\-long\-edge 2048]
One web page with the photo before its edit (framed as the edit is) and after, and a bar to drag between them; both photos are inside the file, so it works offline and on any web host
.TP
.B amb dust <PHOTO> [\-\-line X0,Y0,X1,Y1] [\-\-apply] [\-\-json]
Dust and hairs on a film scan (darker specks and short curved lines on smooth ground; not long straight scratches), each as a heal spot with its donor. Shows them; \-\-apply adds them as one undoable step. Spots already there are kept, and a second run adds only new ones. \-\-line heals a straight scratch along a line (photo fractions, roughly drawn: it moves onto the scratch)
.TP
.B amb stats <PHOTO> [\-\-preset P] [\-\-amount A] [\-\-json]
The photo developed small (with its edit, or a preset) as a few numbers instead of a picture: L* percentiles, clipped shadows and highlights, midtone colour cast, chroma
.TP
.B amb query <SIDECAR.xmp> \-\-queries <QUERIES.json|\->
Answer protocol queries (get_param, list_params, describe, list_groups, list_masks, list_spots) as JSON
.TP
.B amb protocol schema [command|query]
Print the JSON Schema of commands and queries
.TP
.B amb negative analyze <RAW>... [\-\-slides] [\-\-out ROLL.xmp] [\-\-json]
Estimate film base, levels and midtone of scanned negatives (the median over all frames, for a consistent roll) and write them as a preset with Auto off; \-\-slides for slide film
.TP
.B amb negative stocks [\-\-json]
List the built\-in film stock looks
.TP
.B amb lens info <RAW> [\-\-lens\-db DIR] [\-\-lcp\-dir DIR]
Show a raw's lens metadata and the profile it gets
.TP
.B amb lens match \-\-camera\-make X \-\-camera\-model Y \-\-lens\-model M [\-\-lens\-make L] [\-\-focal F] [\-\-aperture A] [\-\-distance D] [\-\-crop C] [\-\-lens\-db DIR] [\-\-lcp\-dir DIR]
Find the lens profile for a shot (Adobe .lcp files you have, then the lensfun database; default locations or AMB_LCP_DIRS / AMB_LENSFUN_DB) and print the models interpolated to its focal length, aperture and distance
.TP
.B amb lens fetch [\-\-to DIR] [\-\-from version_2.tar.bz2] [\-\-force]
Download lensfun's lens database (CC BY\-SA 3.0) from its update server into ~/.local/share/lensfun/updates, where it is found by default; \-\-from installs a downloaded copy
.TP
.B amb models [list] [\-\-json]
The AI models for subject, background and people masks: every freely licensed one we can install, its licence, size and speed, and which is in use (* in use)
.TP
.B amb models install <ID>
Download it (checked against its sha256) into the models folder
.TP
.B amb models use <ID>
Use it for its task's masks (it has to be installed)
.TP
.B amb models add <FILE.onnx> \-\-task subject|people \-\-name NAME \-\-size PX [\-\-mean r,g,b] [\-\-std r,g,b] [\-\-sigmoid|\-\-softmax] [\-\-nhwc] [\-\-channel N] [\-\-invert] [\-\-licence L] [\-\-source URL]
Your own ONNX model: a square RGB photo in, a map of the same side out (or one per class: \-\-channel picks one, \-\-softmax turns scores into shares, \-\-invert flips it; \-\-nhwc for TensorFlow/MediaPipe models); checked that it runs. Guide: docs/own\-models.md
.TP
.B amb models remove <ID>
Delete it; its task goes back to its default
.TP
.B amb import <SOURCE> <DEST> [\-\-into \(dq{yyyy}/{yyyy}\-{mm}\-{dd}\(dq] [\-\-rename \(dq{name}\(dq] [\-\-start 1] [\-\-keywords \(dqa, b\(dq] [\-\-preset LOOK.xmp] [\-\-backup DIR] [\-\-no\-subfolders] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
Copy photos from a card or folder into DEST, sorted into folders and renamed from templates ({name} {yyyy} {yy} {mm} {dd} {hh} {min} {ss} {seq} {camera}); a raw's JPEG and .xmp keep its new name; photos already there are skipped. \-\-preset gives photos without an edit of their own a look; \-\-backup also copies the originals to DIR/Imported on YYYY\-MM\-DD
.TP
.B amb collage list
The built\-in collage layouts
.TP
.B amb collage <LAYOUT> <PHOTO>... \-\-out OUT.jpg [\-\-size WxH] [\-\-background #fff] [\-\-gap 1.5] [\-\-margin 3] [export options]
Several photos (each with its own edit) on one canvas, as the editor's collage maker does: LAYOUT is a built\-in's name or number, or a layout .json. Photos fill the cells by shape; more photos than cells make pages, OUT\-001.jpg, ...
.TP
.B amb catalog scan <DIR>...
Catalogue the photos in DIR and its subfolders: what the library reads from each (rating, keywords, capture time, camera, lens, ...) is kept until the files change, so big folders open quickly. Deleting the catalogue loses nothing
.TP
.B amb catalog find [\-\-text T] [\-\-camera C] [\-\-lens L] [\-\-keyword K] [\-\-rating N] [\-\-from DATE] [\-\-until DATE] [\-\-json]
Search every catalogued photo, newest first
.TP
.B amb catalog stats | forget <DIR>
How many photos it knows; forget a folder (files stay). \-\-catalog FILE uses another catalogue than the editor's
.TP
.B amb catalog add <DIR> | remove <DIR>
Library folders (whole drives too) the editor keeps indexed
.TP
.B amb catalog index
Bring every library folder up to date; an unplugged drive's photos stay listed, offline. \-\-folders FILE: another list
.TP
.B amb catalog folders [\-\-json]
Each catalogued folder with its photo count
.TP
.B amb catalog missing [\-\-json]
Photos whose files are gone from a folder that can be reached (moved or deleted outside Ambrotype)
.TP
.B amb catalog relink <DIR>
Find them in DIR and its subfolders by name and size; the catalogue and collections follow them there
.TP
.B amb info <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-json]
What each photo's sidecar says: rating, label, flag, keywords, title, caption, creator, copyright, place, stack, orientation
.TP
.B amb tag <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-rating 0\-5] [\-\-label Red|...|none] [\-\-flag pick|reject|none] [\-\-add \(dqa, b\(dq] [\-\-remove \(dqc\(dq] [\-\-title T] [\-\-caption C] [\-\-creator C] [\-\-copyright C] [\-\-place LAT,LON|none] [\-\-rotate left|right|180] [\-\-flip horizontal] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
One change to many photos at once, in their sidecars, as the library does it (a place as Lightroom's map writes it, a turn as tiff:Orientation)
.TP
.B amb place <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-gpx TRACK.gpx [\-\-offset HOURS] [\-\-replace] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
Where photos were taken, from a GPS track: \-\-offset is how many hours the camera's clock was ahead of UTC; photos with a place (or the camera's GPS) keep it unless \-\-replace
.TP
.B amb place <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-guess [\-\-within MINUTES] [\-\-clock HOURS] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
Guess places for photos without one from the photos that have one: taken within MINUTES (default 30; between two placed photos, on the line between them), or looking the same (photos Smart search has indexed). \-\-clock: hours the unplaced photos' clock was behind the placed ones'
.TP
.B amb insights <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-by aperture,focal,shutter,iso,hour,camera,lens] [\-\-json]
How the photos were shot: how often each aperture, focal length, shutter speed, ISO, hour, camera and lens comes up, and how many of each were kept (picked or 3 stars and up); then what the numbers suggest and challenges to try
.TP
.B amb cleanup <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-skip dupes,bursts,blurry,eyes,exposure,rejected] [\-\-alike 0\-20] [\-\-burst SECONDS] [\-\-trash|\-\-reject] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
The photos you may not want, each with why: copies and alike pictures (all but the best), the weaker frames of bursts, blurry, eyes closed, nearly black or blown out, rejected; photos picked or rated are left out. \-\-trash moves them to the trash, \-\-reject rejects them
.TP
.B amb duplicates <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-alike 0\-20] [\-\-burst SECONDS] [\-\-stack] [\-\-reject] [\-\-json]
Same files, alike pictures (\-\-alike bits of 64 may differ, default 6; 0: same files only) and bursts (default 2 s), best first; \-\-stack stacks each group with the best on top, \-\-reject picks the best and rejects the rest
.TP
.B amb move <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-to DIR [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]

.TP
.B amb rename <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-name TEMPLATE [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]

.TP
.B amb sort <PHOTO|DIR>... \-\-into DIR [\-\-by \(dq{yyyy}/{yyyy}\-{mm}\-{dd}\(dq] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
Move, rename (Import's tokens: {name} {yyyy} {mm} {dd} {seq} {camera} ...) or sort into dated folders, each photo with its sidecar, JPEG twin and virtual copies; nothing is overwritten (\-2, \-3, ...); the catalogue and collections follow
.TP
.B amb trash <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-dry\-run]
Photos with all their files to the system's trash
.TP
.B amb slideshow <PHOTO|DIR>... [\-\-seconds 1\-600] [\-\-shuffle] [\-\-window] [\-\-subfolders] [\-\-effect none|fade|slide|zoom|black|random]
Opens the editor straight into a slideshow of the photos, each with its edit: 4 s each, a fade, full screen unless \-\-window; random picks a change each time; \-\-subfolders takes in every folder under them. Space pauses, Esc ends
.TP
.B amb keywords [list] [\-\-json] | rename <K>... \-\-to <NEW> | remove <K>... [\-\-dry\-run]
Every keyword in the catalogue with its count; rename, merge or remove keywords in every photo's sidecar
.TP
.B amb collection [list] | show <NAME> | add <NAME> <PHOTO>... | remove <NAME> <PHOTO>... | delete <NAME> [\-\-collections DIR] [\-\-json]
The editor's collections (photos from any folders)
.TP
.B amb lrcat open <CATALOG.lrcat> | close <CATALOG.lrcat> | list [\-\-json]

.TP
.B amb lrcat sample <OUT.lrcat> <PHOTO>...
A small catalogue in Lightroom's layout of these photos (rated 4, Red, picked, Exposure +1, a collection Selects), to try catalogues without Lightroom Open a Lightroom Classic catalogue in place: nothing imported or written. The editor's library and every amb command read its photos' edits, ratings and keywords from it (a sidecar written since wins); its folders and collections show in the library's Folders panel
.TP
.B amb lrcat import <CATALOG.lrcat> [\-\-apply] [\-\-remap OLD=NEW] [\-\-collections DIR] [\-\-json]
Move from Lightroom Classic: each photo's develop settings, rating, label, flag, keywords, stack, title and caption go into its XMP sidecar, virtual copies become ours, and collections (in their sets) the editor's. Shows the plan; \-\-apply writes it. The catalogue is only read (close Lightroom first); sidecars already there are kept. \-\-remap /Volumes/Photos/=/mnt/photos/ finds photos that have moved
.TP
.B amb denoise <RAW>... [\-\-amount 0\-100] [\-\-out OUT.dng] [\-\-json]
AI Denoise: each raw without its noise, as a new DNG beside it (<name>\-Denoised.dng) with the photo's edit; \-\-amount mixes in the photo as it was (default 70) to keep texture; needs the denoise model (amb models install rawnind)
.TP
.B amb merge hdr <RAW>... [\-\-out OUT.dng] [\-\-no\-align] [\-\-deghost low|medium|high] [\-\-json]
Merge bracketed raws of one scene into a floating\-point DNG (default: <first>\-HDR.dng next to them) that opens and edits like a raw, here and in Lightroom; Auto Tone it with amb plugin run plugins/auto\-tone OUT.dng
.TP
.B amb merge pano <RAW>... [\-\-out OUT.dng] [\-\-projection auto|spherical|cylindrical|perspective] [\-\-no\-crop] [\-\-no\-lens] [\-\-lens\-db PATH] [\-\-lcp\-dir DIR] [\-\-json]
Stitch overlapping raws (camera turned about the lens) into a panorama DNG (default: <first>\-Pano.dng next to them), each corrected with its lens profile first; \-\-no\-crop keeps the uncovered edges (black)
.TP
.B amb mcp
Serve the Model Context Protocol over stdio, so your own AI app (Claude Desktop, Claude Code, ...) can edit, preview and export photos with Ambrotype's commands (docs/ai/mcp.md)
.TP
.B amb profile list <RAW> [\-\-dcp\-dir DIR]
List the camera profiles (.dcp) on this computer for a raw's camera (Camera Raw's profile folders, AMB_DCP_DIRS, \-\-dcp\-dir); a preset's or sidecar's CameraProfile picks one by name
.TP
.B amb ref [GROUP]
The core card for AI clients (docs/ai/core.md: the compact syntax and the most used settings), or one group's settings one line each
.TP
.B amb settings reference [\-\-json]
Print the settings reference (docs/ai/settings\-reference.md)
.TP
.B amb docs [NAME...] [\-\-to DIR]
The guides for AI agents, built in: the list, one guide (guide, core, features, settings, mcp, layouts, plugins, …), or all written to DIR with their links working
.TP
.B amb man
Print this help as a manual page (man amb; docs/man/amb.1)
.TP
.B amb plugin new <DIR> [\-\-name \(dqMy plugin\(dq]
Start a plugin project (Rust, built to WebAssembly; docs/ai/plugins.md)
.TP
.B amb plugin build <DIR>
Build it (needs: rustup target add wasm32\-unknown\-unknown), then check it
.TP
.B amb plugin check <DIR>
Validate plugin.json and the module, and run it on a sample
.TP
.B amb plugin run <DIR> <PHOTO|SIDECAR.xmp> [\-\-params a=1,b=Film] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-json]
Run a plugin on a photo's edit and write its sidecar
.SH EXPORT OPTIONS (amb render)
.TP
.B \-\-format jpeg|png|tiff|webp|avif|exr|jxl
Default: from the file extension
.TP
.B \-\-quality 1\-100
JPEG/AVIF quality (default 100)
.TP
.B \-\-bits 8|16|32
PNG 8/16, TIFF 8/16/32 (float); default 8, TIFF 16
.TP
.B \-\-color\-space srgb|p3|adobergb|prophoto|rec2020
Default srgb; an ICC profile is embedded
.TP
.B \-\-long\-edge N | \-\-short\-edge N | \-\-width N | \-\-height N | \-\-fit WxH | \-\-megapixels M | \-\-percent P

.TP
.B \-\-exact WxH
Exactly W×H (e.g. 1080x1350): centre\-cropped if the aspect differs
.TP
.B \-\-enlarge
Allow upscaling (default: never enlarge)
.TP
.B \-\-sharpen screen|matte|glossy[:low|standard|high]
Output sharpening
.TP
.B \-\-metadata all|no\-location|copyright|none
EXIF to include (default no\-location)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-size 500k|2M
JPEG: lower the quality until the file fits
.TP
.B \-\-small\-copy 3M
Also write NAME\-small.jpg, at most that size (as sharp as fits, smaller in pixels only when it must be), for sharing
.TP
.B \-\-subsampling 444|422|420
\-\-progressive  \-\-avif\-speed 1\-10
.TP
.B \-\-rating 1\-5
\-\-keywords \(dqbeach, sunset\(dq   Put a rating and keywords in the file (XMP, IPTC in JPEG, EXIF), with the all / no\-location metadata policies
.TP
.B \-\-border 5%|40px[,#ffffff|auto] | border.json
A frame around the photo; a .json preset can add a deeper bottom, a keyline, rounded corners, and fit (with \-\-exact: the whole photo inside the frame, not cropped)
.TP
.B \-\-border\-caption \(dq{camera} · {exposure}\(dq
A line of text in the border's bottom (made three times the width deep if not set): {camera} {lens} {exposure} {focal} {aperture} {shutter} {iso} {date} {year} {title} {creator} {copyright}
.TP
.B \-\-watermark \(dq© Name\(dq | logo.png | watermark.json
Text or a logo (PNG, its transparency kept) on the photo; \-\-watermark\-at bottom\-right (top\-left, top, top\-right, left, center, right, bottom\-left, bottom), \-\-watermark\-size 20 (% of the width), \-\-watermark\-opacity 70, \-\-watermark\-rotate 30 (degrees), \-\-watermark\-tile (repeat it across the photo)
.PP
Supported inputs: .xmp presets and sidecars, .lrtemplate presets, and files with an embedded XMP packet (e.g. .dng presets for Lightroom mobile). AI and script guide: docs/ai/README.md.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMB_GPU
\fBoff\fR develops on the CPU even when there is a GPU.
.TP
.B AMB_AI_GPU
\fBoff\fR runs the AI models on the CPU.
.TP
.B AMB_MODELS
The folder of AI models (default: the editor's).
.TP
.B AMB_DCP_DIRS
More folders to look for camera profiles (.dcp) in.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I PHOTO.xmp
The sidecar next to each photo: its edit, rating, label, flag, keywords and place, as Lightroom keeps them.
.TP
.I catalog.sqlite
The editor's catalogue, in its config folder: an index of what was read from the photos (deleting it loses nothing).
.SH SEE ALSO
The guide for scripts and AI assistants: docs/ai/README.md in the source, and \fBamb ref\fR. Home: https://github.com/shardpelt/Ambrotype
